The current native build passes all 73 selected scalar specification cases
and 77 core JS API cases with zero unexpected outcomes. Fixes cover C helper argument extension,
floating comparisons, arithmetic NaN canonicalization, saturating conversions,
stack returns and import-wrapper frame allocation. The wrapper frame now
reserves the implicit argument slot required by its call descriptor, matching
PPC/s390 and protecting spills across nested JavaScript calls.
FixedSizeSignature also needs nontrivial copies: SPARC V9 may return trivial
aggregates up to 32 bytes in registers, relocating the object while leaving
its internal pointer aimed at a temporary. Actual-header controls reproduce
the old defect at -O0 and -O3 and pass with the corrected storage ownership.
SegmentedTable::FreelistHead also requires 8-byte alignment for GCC's atomic
compare/exchange expected-value load; the natural 4-byte alignment SIGBUS
negative control and explicitly aligned control document this separately.

