proposal execution. The existing Node/JavaScript JIT regression gates still apply.

Scalar Wasm features (2026-10-29)
---------------------------------

The separate sparc64-wasm-scalar tree starts from the verified atomics
checkpoint node-wasm-atomics-20261029T141122.399167Z. Its parent remains
unchanged. Liftoff PrepareTailCall copies arguments and restores the caller
frame using the SPARC biased stack convention. TailCallIndirect resolves the
code table entry before jumping. The generic call_ref path now loads the
32-bit WasmCodePointer with LoadCodePointer; a full-width load also reads the
neighboring field on a big-endian target. Eight unexpected outcomes from the
atomics-parent binary are resolved by these changes.

The rebuilt T7 binary passes 15 unchanged upstream tail-call, function-reference
and exception suites, and 175 unchanged scalar spec scripts with zero
unexpected outcomes. The upstream expected failures table, memory64/memory64
and memory64/table64 remain unchanged. The frame matrix passes 4,502 checks
across 181 cases and 361 native functions, including mixed scalar/reference
arguments, large frames, multiple return values and 100,000 recursive tail
calls with a 128 KiB stack.

The real application uses the unchanged nlohmann/json v3.11.3 single header
from commit 9cca280a4d0ccf0c08f47a99aa71d1b0e52f8d03, compiled to scalar Wasm
with native C++ exceptions. It normalizes JSON, aggregates a ledger and reports
schema/parse errors. Its 56 cases and 168 invocations are compared with
cross-host and native SPARC GCC oracles. The run catches 15 native C++
exceptions, executes 20,000 tail calls through typed-reference adapters and
grows linear memory. prepare-wasm-scalar-application.py fetches hash-pinned
dependencies; build-wasm-scalar-application.py rebuilds using EMXX, WASM2WAT
and CXX. test-wasm-scalar-acceptance.py repeats native acceptance and builds
the target oracle. The fixture records 504 checks and 15 native functions.

Regression testing exposed a snapshot bug: deserialization passed views(),
which converts a detach-key Cell to kManyViews, into ArrayBuffer Setup. The
one-line fix passes views_or_detach_key() to preserve the Cell. The unfixed
binary builds all four tracking/heap-verification configurations successfully,
but all eight restores fail: key protection is lost, and heap verification
rejects kManyViews when tracking is disabled. After the fix all 12 build/restore
steps pass, as do all 12 original snapshot/cache state cases. The original
binary, failed blob, build metadata and logs are preserved in
out/sparc64-snapshot-before-fix.

test-snapshot-array-buffer-keys.py checks 27 buffers with string, symbol and
object keys, empty/small/large backing stores and different views. Each of four
tracking/heap-verification configurations builds a snapshot and restores it
twice. Restored buffers reject wrong or absent keys, accept the original key,
preserve bytes and invalidate views on detach. A pooled Buffer also keeps its
detach protection. Baseline and fixed runs use identical fixture hashes.

The full inherited regression pipeline passes with the rebuilt binary:
1,010 baseline Wasm checks, 73 preserved spec cases, 77 core JS API cases,
198,392 atomic matrix checks, 372 official atomic spec commands, 14 unchanged
atomic feature suites and the four-worker hash/growth workload; the preserved
6,544-case JavaScript selection, three native RegExp profiles, all 281 Node C++
tests, optimized GC/deoptimization/OSR, addons, snapshots/cache and ten RegExp
snapshot flag configurations; TypeScript/ESLint controls, npm and the two-minute
HTTPS/WebSocket application soak. Node conformance completes 6,061 cases with
zero failures and 478 normal upstream skips: broad 5,831, addons 137, native 93.
Existing explicit JSPI and tool/platform exclusions remain unchanged.

Reproduction on T7 after preparing the application/toolchain inputs:

python3 tools/sparc64/build-wasm.py --incremental
python3 tools/sparc64/test-wasm-scalar-acceptance.py
python3 tools/sparc64/validate-wasm-atomics.py
python3 tools/sparc64/audit-wasm-scalar.py
python3 tools/sparc64/checkpoint.py --profile wasm-scalar

The regression driver includes the detach-key test. The audit requires both
its unchanged-binary negative control and fixed results, checks that the
snapshot rebuild changed only the deserializer source, and requires the
inherited Wasm/atomics/Node/JIT audits and unchanged parent checkpoints.
The scalar checkpoint retains source overlays, binaries, application inputs
and oracles, baseline failures and raw results. Verify it independently with
verify-checkpoint.py and verify its local mirror before closing the goal.
No commits or pushes are performed.

SIMD, comprehensive GC proposal execution, JSPI, optimizing Wasm and additional
debugger/tiering support remain deferred. JavaScript Sparkplug/TurboFan, native
